// 🛋️ The Couch Cast crew (Core deck lobby): a couch on little legs crawls in and sits down, then a
// robot, a dog and an alien wander in, hop onto it, and the robot casts to "the screen", which is
// the QR code card. Now and then one of them gets up and peeks out from behind the QR card, and
// every so often a cat sneaks up to the screen until the dog chases it off. Once in a long while
// a mountain rumbles up beside the couch and Sasquatch strolls down it to fist-bump the crew.
//
// The whole scene is one SVG laid over the lobby *behind* the QR card, so nobody can ever walk in
// front of the code. The couch sits in `stageRef` (the space under the players card), facing the QR
// card (`screenRef`); `qrRef` is the code's own box, which lights up when the cast lands.
//
// Drawing units: each character is ~100 units tall with its feet at (0, 0); the couch is 200 wide.
// The cat is drawn side-on, facing left (it's flipped to run the other way).
//
// 🦇 The Halloween deck runs the same show with its own cast (HalloweenCrew.jsx): a gothic couch, and
// a witch who casts with her wand, the HOA president and a vampire. All three chase off a tiny ghost,
// and Frankenstein's monster comes out of a castle in place of Sasquatch on his mountain. A black chandelier sways above, and
// a few bats fly by now and then.
//
// 📽️ The robot (on every deck but Halloween) casts like a projector: a
// cone of light from its visor lands on the QR code for a few seconds. That light is its own SVG, above the
// cards, since it has to reach the code; it stops at the code's edge so it never covers it.
//
// 🎄 The Holiday deck runs the Core show with the crew dressed up (HolidayCrew.jsx). In place of
// Sasquatch's mountain, Santa lands beside the couch in a sleigh that flies on its own.

// Who sits where, left to right: `caster` is nearest the screen and `chaser` is in the middle
var SEATS = ['caster', 'chaser', 'third'];
var BAT_COUNT = 3;
var HIP = 30; // where a character bends to sit (units up from its feet)
var SEAT_TOP = 44; // the couch cushions' top (units up from the floor)

